#lang rhombus
// The frames a slide comes to rest on.
//
// A slide that has been given stages is an animated `Pict` -- a value from
// rhombus/pict, not a pict this runtime can read. A frame of it is a pict
// again, and the canvases it was built from are still inside that: the tag an
// element carries rides on the pict as a field, so every combinator between
// here and there has kept it.
//
// Which frame, though? Not simply the last: an epoch that fades something out
// ends on a picture with less in it than the one before, and a talk whose last
// beat is a fade-out would come back missing what it faded. So this offers
// every frame the slide settles on -- the start and the end of each epoch --
// and leaves the choice to the caller, which picks the one that shows the most.
//
// This is in Rhombus because `snapshot` is a Rhombus method; everything else
// that reads a slide is Racket, and calls this.
import: pict as pc

export: settle_frames

fun settle_frames(s):
  if s is_a pc.Pict
  | List.append(
      & (for List (i in 0 .. math.max(1, s.duration)):
           [s.snapshot(i, 1.0).handle, s.snapshot(i, 0.0).handle]))
  | [s]
